     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">I&#39;m a long time (old time!) user of the software package Distance, but am\r\nattempting one of my first distance analyses in R and am struggling.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">The data are from the Breeding Bird Survey, and are quite rudimentary in\r\nterms of the information they convey about distance. Two &#39;proper&#39; (closed)\r\ndistance bands of 0-25m and 25-100m, and a third band of &gt;100m. After some thought we are treating this last category as a third closed band of 100-250m (we think this is reasonable for most\r\nof the species we are dealing with).<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">The surveys that generate the data are transects through a 1 km square.\r\n2 x 1km transects are divided into a total of 10 x 200m sections, and the\r\nnumber of each species detected in each section/distance band combination is\r\nrecorded. When more than one bird is recorded, we don&#39;t know whether these\r\nbirds were seen together (i.e. a detection of a group) or separately. We have\r\ndecided to treat each bird detected as a separate detection event (these are,\r\nfor the most part, breeding waders, so they aren&#39;t in large groups and most\r\ndetections will be of individual birds).<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">I&#39;ve attached an example of an attempt at a flatfile format of data for\r\nanalysis of one species (Curlew). <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Each recorded bird gets its own row (as described above we are assuming\r\nall birds are detected independently of one another). The flatfile has the\r\nfollowing columns.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Region.Label</span></b><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">: In my full analysis I have specified several &#39;regions&#39; each defined by\r\na combination of period and whether the data derives from the Max Visit (the\r\nvisit with the most observations) or the Min Visit (with the fewest). However,\r\nin the attached excerpt of example data I have included data from just one of\r\nthese ‘regions’ (Max_Recent).<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </span></b></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Sample.Label</span></b><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">: This contains a unique identifier for every unique combination of\r\nsquare and ‘region’.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">distance</span></b><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">: The mid-point of the relevant distance band (i.e. 12.5, 62.5 or 175). In\r\naddition to a row for every bird recorded on the survey (with a valid entry in\r\nthe &#39;distance&#39; column), there is a &#39;blank&#39; row (with NA in the distance column)\r\nfor every survey carried out where no birds were detected. This is to make sure\r\nthat surveys with no detections are taken into account.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Effort</span></b><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">: Twice the total number of visits contributing data to the\r\nSample.Label. Each survey visit comprises two 1km long transects. <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Area</span></b><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">: Because the Regions are actually periods, they each cover the entire\r\nsurvey area. Area is therefore the total land area of the UK, from which BBS\r\nsquares are drawn.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">The following code opens the relevant packages, sets up cutpoints,\r\nimports the data and runs the mode. The tic and toc commands, from package &#39;tictoc&#39;, return the time taken for the intervening code to run:<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">library (Distance)<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">library (tictoc)<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">Cuts &lt;- c(0,025,100,250)<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">BBS_Example &lt;- read.csv(&quot;Example_BBS_data.csv&quot;)<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">tic(&quot;Example_run&quot;)<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">CU_hn_example &lt;- ds(BBS_Example, transect = &quot;line&quot;,\r\ntruncation = 250,cutpoints = Cuts)<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">toc()<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">summary(CU_hn_example)</font><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">When I run this, I get the following messages</span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Starting\r\nAIC adjustment term selection.<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Fitting\r\nhalf-normal key function<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Key\r\nonly model: not constraining for monotonicity.<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">AIC=\r\n15128.692<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Fitting\r\nhalf-normal key function with cosine(2) adjustments<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">AIC=\r\n15102.384<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Fitting\r\nhalf-normal key function with cosine(2,3) adjustments<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">AIC=\r\n15096.218<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Fitting\r\nhalf-normal key function with cosine(2,3,4) adjustments<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">AIC=\r\n15092.369<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Fitting\r\nhalf-normal key function with cosine(2,3,4,5) adjustments<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">AIC=\r\n15094.369<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><u></u><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> </font><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Half-normal\r\nkey function with cosine(2,3,4) adjustments selected.<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Error in t(partial) %*% vcov : non-conformable arguments</font></span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;color:blue\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">&gt;\r\ntoc()<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">\r\n\r\n</font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;color:black;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0cm\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Example_run:\r\n302.67 sec elapsed</font><font face=\"Lucida Console\"><u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;color:black;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0cm\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;color:black;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0cm\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">The distribution of observations between distance bands </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13.3333px\">(see attached simple figure)</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\"> looks sensible enough to me for a bird like Curlew, for which calls can be heard over 100s of metres. All units (relating to both area and distance) are in metres. Any advice would be hugely appreciated. Apologies if I&#39;ve omitted any necessary information to diagnose this problem - please let me know and I&#39;ll provide whatever I can.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size